# Paths that never enter a Docker build context (BETA-P0-017).
#
# Every image builds with the repository root as its context. No Dockerfile
# copies these today; excluding them means none can by accident, and the files
# are not even sent to the builder.
#
# The web tier's TLS certificate, private key, and the staged and previous
# copies scripts/tls-install.sh writes beside them.
infrastructure/docker/nginx/tls/
# ACME challenge tokens: not secret, but host state, not source.
infrastructure/docker/nginx/acme-webroot/

# Secrets and host state (private-beta security audit). The Dockerfiles copy
# whole service directories, so a `.env` or a credential that ends up inside
# one would otherwise ship in the image. Nothing copies any of these today.
.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
infrastructure/kind/generated/
infrastructure/observability/secrets/
infrastructure/observability/alertmanager/secrets/
backups/
# Per-run secrets e2e/stack.sh generates for the browser E2E stack.
e2e/.stack/

# Host build state (release-engineering audit). Every image installs its own
# dependencies with `npm ci` inside the build and builds its own bundle, so none
# of this is ever needed — but the Dockerfiles copy whole workspace directories
# (`COPY services/observability services/observability`), and a workspace's own
# node_modules on the host (npm nests a package there when versions differ:
# services/observability/node_modules/prom-client today) was copied over the one
# `npm ci` had just installed in the image — host-built, and on a Mac built for
# the wrong platform if it were ever a native addon. It was also ~270 MB of
# context sent to the builder on every build.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
e2e/test-results/
e2e/playwright-report/
